{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>ואהי נגוע</b> — by the wicked. And the yod of ותוכחתי is a sign of the object, for the wicked reprove him — the opposite of ותוכחתי לא אביתם, where it is a sign of the subject. And in my opinion: נגוע is from the side of its head to bear its suffering to subdue his impulse, ותוכחתי לנפשי (my chastisement is upon myself)." "<b>וטעם לבקרים</b> — every morning, as in: חדשים לבקרים."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {0 "The phrase 'מפאת ראשו לסבלו' is obscure; read hyper-literally. The interplay between the two instances of ותוכחתי (one as object-marked, one as subject-marked) drives the argument but the syntax is compressed."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:17.118712243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}